  "body": "Support SVG and MathML namespaces for `<template>` elements\n\nAllow `<template>` elements to parse their template contents in the HTML, SVG, or MathML namespace, either explicitly via `contentnamespace` or implicitly from their context:\n\n- Add a sticky `template content namespace` internal slot on `<template>` (defaulting to the HTML namespace) and `HTMLTemplateElement.prototype.contentNamespace` to get and set it as a namespace URL (`\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"`, `\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"`, or `\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"`, throwing a `TypeError` for other values).\n- Add the enumerated `contentnamespace=\"html|svg|mathml\"` content attribute (consulted during HTML and XML parsing), and allow `contentnamespace` in the built-in safe default Sanitizer configuration.\n- Allow `<template>` elements as children of SVG elements (other than `script` and `style`) and MathML elements (ignored for MathML content models, layout, and rendering).\n- When `contentnamespace` is missing or invalid at parse time (HTML and XML), inherit the namespace from the parser context (`<svg>`/`<math>` ancestors, `<template for>` patch targets, or fragment context), treating HTML and MathML text integration points as HTML-namespace contexts (checking live `encoding` on `<annotation-xml>` outside an active HTML parser) and clamping other or null namespaces to HTML.\n- `shadowrootmode` overrides `template content namespace` to HTML when `attach a shadow root` succeeds.\n- In `prepare content patching` (`<template for>`), inherit the patch target's namespace when `contentnamespace` is missing or invalid, and error the patch if an explicit `contentnamespace` mismatches the target.\n- In HTML fragment serialization, always emit `contentnamespace=\"html|svg|mathml\"` first on `<template>` elements and skip any existing `contentnamespace` attribute so namespaces round-trip.\n- Allow `<template/>` to be self-closing in foreign content, and stop foreign end-tag recovery at open `<template>` boundaries (preserving HTML fallback at non-`<template>` fragment roots).\n\nTests: https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/63892.\n\nCloses #12976\nCloses #3563\n---\n\n- [ ] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\n   * …\n   * …\n- [x] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at:\n   * https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/63892\n- [ ] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are filed:\n   * Chromium: …\n   * Gecko: …\n   * WebKit: …\n- [x] Corresponding [HTML AAM](https://w3c.github.io/html-aam/) & [ARIA in HTML](https://w3c.github.io/html-aria/) issues & PRs: N/A\n- [ ] [MDN issue](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) is filed: …\n- [x] The top of this comment includes a [clear commit message](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/COMMITTING.md) to use.\n\n(See [WHATWG Working Mode: Changes](https://whatwg.org/working-mode#changes) for more details.)\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13100/dynamic-markup-insertion.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 19, 2026, 4:45 PM UTC (4831098)\">/dynamic-markup-insertion.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13100/0793d3d...4831098/dynamic-markup-insertion.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 19, 2026, 4:45 PM UTC (4831098)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13100/embedded-content-other.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 19, 2026, 4:45 PM UTC (4831098)\">/embedded-content-other.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13100/0793d3d...4831098/embedded-content-other.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 19, 2026, 4:45 PM UTC (4831098)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13100/indices.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 19, 2026, 4:45 PM UTC (4831098)\">/indices.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13100/0793d3d...4831098/indices.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 19, 2026, 4:45 PM UTC (4831098)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13100/infrastructure.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 19, 2026, 4:45 PM UTC (4831098)\">/infrastructure.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13100/0793d3d...4831098/infrastructure.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 19, 2026, 4:45 PM UTC (4831098)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13100/parsing.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 19, 2026, 4:45 PM UTC (4831098)\">/parsing.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13100/0793d3d...4831098/parsing.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 19, 2026, 4:45 PM UTC (4831098)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13100/scripting.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 19, 2026, 4:45 PM UTC (4831098)\">/scripting.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13100/0793d3d...4831098/scripting.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 19, 2026, 4:45 PM UTC (4831098)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13100/syntax.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 19, 2026, 4:45 PM UTC (4831098)\">/syntax.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13100/0793d3d...4831098/syntax.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 19, 2026, 4:45 PM UTC (4831098)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13100/xhtml.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 19, 2026, 4:45 PM UTC (4831098)\">/xhtml.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13100/0793d3d...4831098/xhtml.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 19, 2026, 4:45 PM UTC (4831098)\">diff</a> )",
